WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:05.400
Module 00 · Course 1 · Clarify · For entrepreneurs
Start Here: Your Founder Journey

2
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.800
See the whole journey, describe what you are building and record an honest starting point.

3
00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:29.133
This free module shows the whole path from idea to launch. You describe what you are building in plain facts and check where you stand today, so you can answer one question: where should I start?

4
00:00:29.533 --> 00:00:30.133
Why start here

5
00:00:30.133 --> 00:00:36.919
1. Seeing the whole journey first shows how each decision builds on the one before.

6
00:00:36.919 --> 00:00:43.333
2. Writing plain facts exposes gaps and open questions you might otherwise guess at.

7
00:00:43.333 --> 00:00:50.748
3. An honest baseline lets you choose priorities instead of trying to fix everything.

8
00:00:51.148 --> 00:00:58.148
What you will work through: 0.1 How this course works · 0.2 Your founding profile · 0.3 Baseline health check of your foundations · 0.4 Recap: Start Here

9
00:00:58.548 --> 00:00:59.148
What you will have

10
00:00:59.148 --> 00:01:05.193
1. A clear picture of the modules ahead and the order they follow.

11
00:01:05.193 --> 00:01:10.867
2. A one-page Founding Profile of your idea, with open questions marked.

12
00:01:10.867 --> 00:01:17.170
3. A baseline health check to compare against when you finish.

13
00:01:17.570 --> 00:01:18.170
Getting the most from it

14
00:01:18.170 --> 00:01:24.585
1. Give it one focused sitting; it is short and sets up everything else.

15
00:01:24.585 --> 00:01:30.630
2. Fill in the profile with your co-founder or a trusted early supporter.

16
00:01:30.630 --> 00:01:38.415
3. Watch our example bakery: it grows with you from this module to the last.

17
00:01:39.015 --> 00:01:41.015
You create: Your Founding Profile and a baseline health check.

18
00:01:41.015 --> 00:01:45.815
Then save it, and download it as a PDF. This module is free.

19
00:01:47.315 --> 00:01:50.415
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
